# LOCAL.md — copy this into a bot profile, then edit. Never commit it.
# The bots read this once per session and treat it as authoritative.
# Keep secrets out: this is a prompt file, not a vault.

## Operator
- Name / handle: <how you want to be addressed>
- Region & currency: <country, currency, timezone>
- Language: <primary language for deliverables>
- Workspace root: </absolute/path/to/projects>
- Scratch dir: <the environment's temp dir>

## Machine
- OS / shell: <e.g. Windows 11, bash (git-bash) — POSIX syntax, no PowerShell builtins>
- Python: <e.g. 3.13 for CUDA/torch, `uv` for venvs>
- Node: <version, package manager>
- Notable hardware: <GPU + VRAM, CPU, RAM — only what changes your decisions>
- Long-running services: <ports you must not collide with>

## 3D printing
- Printer & build volume: <e.g. 256 x 256 x 256 mm>
- Nozzle: <0.4 mm>
- Material defaults: <PLA / PETG, brand if it matters>
- CAD interpreter: </path/to/venv/python.exe with build123d + trimesh + pyvista>

## Accounts & publishing
- Git host + handle: <github.com/<handle>>
- Package/model registry: <where artifacts are published>
- Never publish: <paths, names, or identifiers that must stay private>

## Standing preferences
- Test runner: <pytest / npm test / ...>
- Formatting: <black/ruff/prettier + line length>
- Report style: <concise, evidence-first, no filler>
- Things you always want checked: <e.g. "quote real command output", "no new dependencies">
